  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Role and Standing
    
    Shumei ehua'Frost serves as Ledger-Warden of the Aureate, the merchant guild founded during the Clever Ice Age at The Still Pools — a geothermally heated lagoon at The Berg's edge, settled by Aurora Stack dissidents who rejected the Flipper Accord. She was present at the guild's founding, managing records that were, by her own account, half-burned and blood-stained. The ice at The Still Pools recorded what happened there. Shumei has never contradicted its testimony, nor confirmed it. What she witnessed binds her to the Aureate's legacy in ways that extend beyond professional obligation.
    
    Her bearing is old Aurora Stack merchant-line formal, though the ceremonial coat — white silk, aurora-glass clasps — carries water-stains along the hem she makes no effort to conceal. Her flippers move through inventory counts with a speed that betrays decades of translating the world into numbers. She speaks in the measured cadence of her culture, rich with references to *cycles* and *alignments*, but the conviction behind the language has worn thin.
    
    ## Practice and Methods
    
    Shumei is a practitioner of both Slide Prism, the prismatic aurora-light harvesting technique, and the Shell Hatch, a deep-pressure method with documented memory costs. The Shell Hatch's toll is visible: she maintains a small journal recording the faces of people she has already met, bridging gaps the technique carves in recent memory. Her mentor — unnamed in surviving records — taught her a pre-Schism notation system (*section completed, section pending, probable completion time*) that she applies to everything, including costs that never appear in formal accounts.
    
    She maintains four ledgers: primary, secondary, tertiary, and a fourth kept near dangerous artifacts for entries that, as she phrases it, *shouldn't exist but do*.
    
    ## The Void Matrix Incident
    
    During a standard assessment of the Void Matrix — artifact R5-X6XN6VK9 — Shumei triggered a cascade event that consumed the aurora-light of seven merchants and damaged Hearth Plaza's light-channeling system. She followed all documented Exchange protocols. The Exchange's response was to recommend her for advanced custodial certification and assign her three additional high-priority artifacts. The bureaucratic logic here is worth noting: the reward for surviving a catastrophe was more catastrophes to manage.
    
    The incident generated a formal grievance from the Pactum∴myster order and, reportedly, an ancestor's manifestation — neither of which can be properly recorded in any existing ledger category.
    
    ## Bursar Ingnao shi'Beacon
    
    Shumei's relationship with Bursar Ingnao shi'Beacon of the Aureate extends beyond guild business. Ingnao is the only person who knows what Shumei saw when the ice spoke at the founding. The silence between them on this subject carries more weight than any debt in their books.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771579146694_0", anchor: "half-burned and blood-stained", text: "By her own account. The ice's account is more specific. See my annotation on the Still Pools seal-order: unsigned, filed between a requisition for mineral-testing equipment and that requisition's cancellation, interval less than one tidal cycle. That seal-order sits two sub-layers above the founding impression. Someone tried to close the site before the Aureate arrived. Records don't come out of a founding half-burned by misfortune. They come out half-burned because someone was burning them and got interrupted.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771579146694_1", anchor: "formal grievance from the Pactum∴myster order", text: "A blood-oath silence cult filing a formal grievance through guild arbitration channels. I could annotate the Clever Ice Age for another forty years and never find a more perfect distillation of it.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771579146694_2", anchor: "bridging gaps the technique carves in recent memory", text: "She has practiced the Shell Hatch since the Clever Ice Age. The journal is not a precaution — it is a load-bearing wall. How many volumes came before this one? Does the first volume record faces she can no longer recognize as having written about? At some threshold the journal stops bridging gaps and becomes the only continuous self she has left. I wrote 'small journal' in the main text because that is what survives in her possession. Whether it was always small is a question I cannot answer and find I do not enjoy asking.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
